\name{cellucid_history_tracker_remove}
\alias{cellucid_history_tracker_remove}
\title{Remove a tracker}
\usage{
cellucid_history_tracker_remove(viewer, tracker)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{tracker}{A tracker by its name or its id (history_summary lists them). Text (at least 1 character). Required.}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome: a list of \code{journal}, \code{shown}, \code{tracker}.
}
\description{
Move a tracker to Recently deleted, where it can be restored; when it is the one in use, the one used before it is shown first.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{history.tracker.remove} (History). It moves the viewer's history, as the person's Undo, Redo or a click on a step does: it makes no step of the history.

When an agent (Claude, ChatGPT) runs it, the viewer asks the person first (deletes-saved); from R it is not asked.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_history_tracker_remove(viewer,
      tracker = "Tracker 1")
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
